--- ISSUE 7/11 ---
id: UND-002
severity: moderate
category: a11y-understandable
found_by: static
related: RSP-001 (cite the same line — one edit may resolve all)
title: Give every page a descriptive title
problem: 2 document(s) with a missing or empty <title> — the title names the tab, bookmark, and history entry.
why_it_matters: The <title> is the first thing screen readers announce and the text shown in browser tabs; a vague or duplicate title disorients users.
standards: wcag:2.4.2, html:H25
locations:
  - legacy/prototype/design-ref.html:1 ~67f0
       1| <style> <<<
       2|     :root {
       3|         --neo-page-bg: #fff;
       4| 
  - legacy/prototype/scripts/graph-block.html:1
       1|  <<<
       2|       // ----------------------------------------------------------------
       3|       // Dependency tree — tidy horizontal node-link (Redux-DevTools style).
       4|       //
fix: Add a concise, descriptive <title> to each document.

