--- ISSUE 9/11 ---
id: PRF-003
severity: minor
category: performance
found_by: static
title: Set font-display for web fonts
problem: 1 @font-face without font-display — text can stay invisible during font load (FOIT).
why_it_matters: Without font-display, web fonts can block text rendering until fully downloaded, harming FCP and user-perceived speed. Using swap or optional avoids an invisible-text period.
standards: cwv:FCP
locations:
  - apps/ui-remix/src/styles/app.css:19:1 ~6913
      16| /* Mona Sans Fallback — sized to match the variable file's metrics so
      17|    first paint doesn't re-flow when the real font lands. The size-adjust
      18|    number was tuned against the Mona Sans 400 weight for a clean swap. */
      19| @font-face { <<<
      20|   font-family: 'Mona Sans Fallback';
      21|   src: local('Helvetica Neue'), local('Arial');
      22|   ascent-override: 95%;
fix: Add font-display: swap (or optional) to every @font-face rule.

